From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 3ds-d2 <3ds-d2@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:48:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cooperative scheduler: a wait with timeout 0 returns at once

WaitForSingleObject(h, 0) and its kin are polls: on Windows they return
WAIT_TIMEOUT at once when the object is not signaled, without blocking or
yielding. The cooperative scheduler blocked them until the next millisecond
of virtual time, so each poll of an unsignaled object cost a millisecond or
more, and an idle sleep of the host when no other guest thread could run.

Diablo II polls each of its pending file loads every frame (0x40a7f0), and
its event pool polls its events to find a free one (0x40a550). On a New 3DS
the drawing thread spent 1.3 to 2.7 s of the slowest 10 s play windows
blocked in those polls (3ds-d2 issue #31).

A wait with timeout 0 that cannot acquire its object now returns 0x102;
wait_timeout_result returns its own timeout value for it. Sleep(0) still
yields (wx86_wait_sleep).
---
 src/runtime/sched_cooperative.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 src/runtime/sched_cooperative.h   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 mode change 100644 => 100755 src/runtime/sched_cooperative.cpp
 mode change 100644 => 100755 src/runtime/sched_cooperative.h

diff --git a/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.cpp b/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.cpp
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index 8267e7b..274414f
--- a/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.cpp
@@ -150,6 +150,14 @@ uint32_t CooperativeScheduler::wait(Waitable* w, uint32_t timeout_ms) {
 #else
     if (w->try_acquire(cur_)) return w->result();   // already signaled
 #endif
+    // A poll (timeout 0) returns WAIT_TIMEOUT at once, without blocking or
+    // yielding, as on Windows. Blocking it until the next millisecond made
+    // every poll of an unsignaled event cost a millisecond or more, and an
+    // idle sleep of the host when no other guest thread could run: a game
+    // polling each of its pending file loads every frame spent seconds of
+    // a ten-second window there. Sleep(0) yields on its own path
+    // (wx86_wait_sleep).
+    if (timeout_ms == 0) return 0x102;
     cur_->wait_obj = w;
     // Real-time mode: virt_ms_ is only pulled up to the host clock when a
     // thread is picked, so after a long slice it lags real time and a deadline
@@ -160,8 +168,7 @@ uint32_t CooperativeScheduler::wait(Waitable* w, uint32_t timeout_ms) {
     // WaitForSingleObject actually time out under the cooperative scheduler —
     // e.g. a render worker waiting on a frame event must still wake up to
     // keep producing, or a thread blocked on it forever would deadlock.
-    cur_->wake_deadline = (timeout_ms == 0xFFFFFFFFu) ? 0
-                          : virt_ms_ + (timeout_ms ? timeout_ms : 1);
+    cur_->wake_deadline = (timeout_ms == 0xFFFFFFFFu) ? 0 : virt_ms_ + timeout_ms;
     cur_->state = S::Blocked;
     br_->request_yield();                           // stop resumably; scheduler switches
     return 0;                                        // placeholder; EAX set to result on wake
diff --git a/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.h b/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.h
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index 22615ee..060b68f
--- a/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.h
+++ b/src/runtime/sched_cooperative.h
@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@ public:
     uint32_t wait_timeout_result(Waitable* w, uint32_t timeout_ms, uint32_t eax_on_timeout) override {
         uint32_t r = wait(w, timeout_ms);
         if (cur_ && cur_->state == GuestThread::State::Blocked) cur_->wake_timeout_eax = eax_on_timeout;
+        else if (timeout_ms == 0 && r == 0x102) return eax_on_timeout;   // a poll that timed out at once
         return r;   // placeholder in coop (EAX rewritten on wake) — see interface doc
     }
     void notify(Waitable* w) override;
